  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Added a source-transparent packed CSR connected-components kernel and routed heavy public Graph/DiGraph weak-component traversals through one native/Wasm call while retaining the exact edge-scan oracle and explicit portable route evidence. Exact CPython, JavaScript, inspected-core, public-workflow, real Node-WASI, invalid-input, batching, and performance tests pass; the matched-median benchmark measures a 5.16x same-source speedup and the authenticated public Wasm route reports one crossing.",
    "risks": [
      "The 100000 vertex-edge-scan threshold is intentionally conservative and was profiled on sparse cycles; future browser telemetry may justify engine- or density-aware tuning without changing semantics.",
      "Aggregate Wasm capability and production-kernel registries are shared integration surfaces and may need deterministic regeneration if other fast-math lanes land first."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Merge the explicit graph lane-policy prerequisite before this implementation lane, then reconcile shared registry totals with other lanes.",
      "Rebuild the flint-wasm production native-kernel packs so the registered graph core is included in the shipped browser assets, and retain the cross-engine browser parity pass in the integration lane."
    ]
  }
